// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
// Shipped defaults — /etc/eclipse/abyss.kdl. Owned by the image (D-01 §4.1):
// a package upgrade replaces this file wholesale and it is deliberately not
// listed in backup=(), so it must stay pristine. Your changes belong in
// ~/.config/eclipse/abyss.kdl, which is applied after this file.
//
// This file is nearly empty on purpose. A default that lives in a config file
// is a default you have to delete to get back to; a default that lives in the
// schema is one you never see. Everything abyss ships is in the schema.

// The terminal bind used to live here on the theory that the schema cannot
// know what is installed, but eclipseos-meta installs foot, so the schema can
// and does know. A default stated in two places is a default that drifts.
//
// The one exception is a window rule: rules are a list, not a schema key, and
// every file's rules are appended, so yours still apply after these and a
// later `tile` rule for the same app-id overrides this one.

// wl-copy (wl-clipboard) cannot use data control, which is allowlist-only
// (ADR 0022), so it maps a throwaway toplevel just to get keyboard focus,
// sets the selection and destroys it at once. Tiled, it squeezes the
// neighbouring tiles for a frame on every copy — and a terminal that copies
// on select runs it constantly. Float only: it needs the keyboard focus, so
// no `no-focus-steal`.
windowrule "float" { app-id "^io\\.github\\.bugaevc\\.wl-clipboard$"; }
